WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:17.726
The old man told everyone about Dr. Dolittle.

2
00:00:17.727 --> 00:00:21.295
Everyone wanted to bring their animals to him.

3
00:00:21.296 --> 00:00:26.201
Soon Dr. Dolittle became known as the animal doctor.

4
00:00:26.202 --> 00:00:33.234
His sister, Sarah, was happy again because now they had plenty of money.

5
00:00:33.235 --> 00:00:36.060
Farmers came from miles away to see him.

6
00:00:36.061 --> 00:00:40.712
"I don't know what's wrong with him, Doctor," one murmured.

7
00:00:40.713 --> 00:00:46.417
"I've been trying to tell him for weeks now!" the horse complained.

8
00:00:46.418 --> 00:00:47.831
"You must be patient.

9
00:00:47.832 --> 00:00:57.640
He doesn't understand," Dr. Dolittle gently reminded the animal.

10
00:00:57.641 --> 00:01:01.204
"That's the problem with humans!" said the horse.

11
00:01:01.205 --> 00:01:03.765
"They just don't listen!"

12
00:01:03.766 --> 00:01:09.039
"Now, now, let's take a look at you," the doctor kindly replied.

13
00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:16.494
"Look! He's giving me pills for diarrhea!"

14
00:01:16.495 --> 00:01:20.121
The doctor soon realized the horse's problem.

15
00:01:20.122 --> 00:01:24.645
"You have poor eyesight," Dr. Dolittle said.

16
00:01:24.646 --> 00:01:32.104
"YES! I need glasses, not diarrhea pills!" he sighed with relief.

17
00:01:32.105 --> 00:01:36.714
"I'll get you a pair then," and he wrote in his notebook.

18
00:01:36.715 --> 00:01:40.115
"I like yours. Can I get some like that?"

19
00:01:40.116 --> 00:01:43.256
the horse nudged Dr. Dolittle's glasses.

20
00:01:43.257 --> 00:01:45.041
"Yes, they are rather nice.

21
00:01:45.042 --> 00:01:49.795
I'll see what I can do," said Dr. Dolittle.

22
00:01:49.796 --> 00:01:53.914
A week later, the horse returned with the farmer.

23
00:01:53.915 --> 00:01:56.273
"I got green glasses for you,"

24
00:01:56.274 --> 00:01:59.712
Dr. Dolittle said as he put them on.

25
00:01:59.713 --> 00:02:02.878
"I just love the color green!

26
00:02:02.879 --> 00:02:06.544
Thank you!" he smiled.

27
00:02:06.545 --> 00:02:08.518
"There! How's that?

28
00:02:08.519 --> 00:02:11.980
Can you see better?" asked the doctor.

29
00:02:11.981 --> 00:02:18.635
"Crystal clear! You really are amazing, Dr. Dolittle,"said the horse.

30
00:02:18.636 --> 00:02:26.612
Soon it was not unusual to see horses wearing glasses around Puddleby.

31
00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:31.339
All the animals told their family and friends about Dr. Dolittle.

32
00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.603
His garden was always crowded with animals.

33
00:02:34.604 --> 00:02:42.042
There were so many that Dr. Dolittle put up signs for each animal.

34
00:02:42.043 --> 00:02:45.666
"All cows stand here! Horses, there!

35
00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:50.514
Sheep, over there, please!" Polynesia called out.

36
00:02:50.515 --> 00:02:54.061
Dr. Dolittle's other pets helped him, too.

37
00:02:54.062 --> 00:02:56.148
"Hey! It's not your turn!

38
00:02:56.149 --> 00:03:00.954
Get back in line," Jip growled to a straying cow.

39
00:03:00.955 --> 00:03:07.834
"Okay, next horse, please come this way," Gub-Gub called out.

40
00:03:07.835 --> 00:03:11.621
Dr. Dolittle saw the bigger animals in his garden.

41
00:03:11.622 --> 00:03:14.811
His office was for the smallest of creatures.

42
00:03:14.812 --> 00:03:21.975
Mice, raccoons, badgers, and squirrels all waited in line to see the doctor.

43
00:03:21.976 --> 00:03:28.057
"You've got to stop eating food from the garbage," Dr. Dolittle told a little mouse.

44
00:03:28.058 --> 00:03:31.781
"But I'm hungry!" the mouse cried.

45
00:03:31.782 --> 00:03:35.865
Try to find something fresh like fruits or vegetables then."

46
00:03:35.866 --> 00:03:40.605
The mouse felt better after taking some medicine.

47
00:03:40.606 --> 00:03:46.154
Every night Dr. Dolittle was very tired but he was very happy.

48
00:03:46.155 --> 00:03:50.506
"You're famous all over Puddleby," said Gub-Gub.

49
00:03:50.507 --> 00:03:56.148
"Famous all over the world," Too-Too hooted.

50
00:03:56.149 --> 00:04:00.842
"Some friends of mine from England have heard of you," explained the owl.

51
00:04:00.843 --> 00:04:05.704
"If only more humans could speak our language," sighed Jip.

52
00:04:05.705 --> 00:04:11.489
"Still, there would never be anyone like Dr. Dolittle," Polynesia remarked.

53
00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:27.585
"ZZZZZZ . . . ," the doctor mumbled.
